Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 23:31:23 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(docs): make the first 4-axis part model match the
 round ends of its flats

PR #2135 review: the model had square-ended flats from X-0.875 to
X-0.125, but the 1/4 in tool cuts each flat in one pass and leaves round
ends, so the model was up to 0.0117 in below the real part there.

- gen_first_4axis_part_obj.py builds the skin as lines along X with the
  round flat ends; the .obj and the model in the project are regenerated.
  The posted program is unchanged.
- the_model_is_the_bar_as_the_program_cuts_it compares the model with
  the surface the cached toolpaths leave, on a grid over each of the
  four faces, and at the reviewer's point (X-0.87, 0.05 in off centre).
- The page and the decision file state the round ends.

Refs #1904

